  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Circular Economy and Waste Management UGA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda is facing a growing waste management crisis due to rapid urbanization, increased consumption, and inadequate infrastructure, with projections indicating a 70% rise in waste generation by 2050. Current systems are overstretched, especially in cities like Kampala, leading to environmental and public health issues. Existing policies are fragmented and lack effective coordination.To address these challenges, the project proposes establishing a National Multistakeholder Platform for Waste Mana</narrative>
  </description>
